One particular obscure title (in the USA, anyway,) that is roguelike and 
is quite a bit of fun is Monster Gate for the Game Boy Advance, by 
Konami. Thus far it has only been published in Japan and in Japanese, 
but the game is very visual, and the concepts are very easy to 
understand, especially if you are into roguelikes. A couple of English 
faqs on the game are available on gamefaqs.
I liked it a lot and found the gameplay engaging, sometimes almost TOO 
engaging (the SLOT MACHINES...) It mostly holds true to the concepts of 
roguelikes but more simplified, with lots of bells and whistles that 
actually do add to the game enjoyment, rather than just dress it up.

Another simple roguelike is Beneath Apple Manor for the Apple II series 
of computers, if you're into that sort of thing...

